Hi all, I'm a spanish programmer (<a href="http://trinit.es" class="postlink">http://trinit.es</a>) and I'm new in this forum.<br><br>I have been working with Bullet library under Bennu (<a href="http://bennugd.org" class="postlink">http://bennugd.org</a>) for many weeks and I love this engine. I have used almost all working functions on Bennu and I'm really fascinated, but Bullet library for Bennu (Which is really GREAT) is not 100% tested and some advanced functions don't work properly, like antialiasing for example and some physics.<br><br>I'd like to start programming with "native" Bullet, but I don't know how to start... C++, Java..?<br><br>Do you have a project "template" which could work on CodeBlocks? I mean, a VERY simple project with a cube model and a camera, nothing more (Less than 50 lines of code?).<br><br>A .zip file with <span style="text-decoration:underline">all libraries</span> included on a CodeBlocks project would be great, so it could be just compiled and run without the "usual compiling errors" and start working with it... I hope anyone could help with this, it would be very helpfull for beginners (Like me <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":D" title="Very Happy">) and I think it would be used a lot.<br><br>Very very thanks and happy coding <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_razz.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":P" title="Razz"><br><br><strong class="text-strong">EDIT</strong>: Sorry if my english is a little "blurry".. :S<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6235">Windgate</a> — Sat Jan 23, 2010 5:39 pm</p><hr />
